# Ubuntu 24.04 with what CI's `sway` job installs (sway 1.9): podman build -t chatmon-sway19 -f Containerfile .
# from a folder holding this file and a copy of packaging/requirements-test.txt. run.sh runs the tests in it.
FROM docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04
ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
# CI's sway job's packages, plus what the runner image already has that Qt's wheels need, and a Python with venv.
RUN apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq --no-install-recommends \
      sway grim wl-clipboard dbus at-spi2-core python3-gi gir1.2-atspi-2.0 libegl1 libgl1 libxkbcommon0 libfontconfig1 \
      libdbus-1-3 libwayland-client0 libwayland-cursor0 libwayland-egl1 wayland-protocols \
      python3 python3-venv ca-certificates fonts-dejavu-core libglib2.0-0t64 libfreetype6 libx11-6 libxcb1 libx11-xcb1 \
      libxkbcommon-x11-0 libxrender1 libxi6 libsm6 libice6 libopengl0 libgssapi-krb5-2 \
    > /dev/null && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
COPY requirements-test.txt /tmp/requirements-test.txt
RUN python3 -m venv /venv && /venv/bin/pip install -q --require-hashes -r /tmp/requirements-test.txt
RUN useradd -m tester
